The **Rust Foundation** is a non-profit [membership organization](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Membership_organization) incorporated in [United States](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States); it manages the Rust trademark, infrastructure, and assets.[206][49]

It was established on February 8, 2021.[207] The foundation's board was chaired by Shane Miller,[208] with Ashley Williams as interim executive director.[49] In late 2021, Rebecca Rumbul became executive director and CEO.[209]

The foundation's website lists ARM, Amazon, Google, Huawei, Meta, Microsoft, and OpenAI as platinum members.[210] OpenAI is the latest platinum member, having joined in June 2026.[47]

